          "text": "Dear Colleague,\n\nHistory of Present Illness:\nThe patient has focal epilepsy with focal-to-bilateral tonic-clonic seizures. Seizure onset occurred at age 29 years. The current seizure frequency is approximately two per week. The epilepsy has a genetic etiology associated with a pathogenic PCDH19 variant, c.918G>A. The epilepsy is drug responsive.\n\nCurrent Antiseizure Medications:\n- Zonisamide\n- Lamotrigine\n\nSeizure Burden Summary:\nFocal-to-bilateral tonic-clonic seizures occurring approximately twice weekly.\n\nAssessment:\nDrug-responsive focal epilepsy of genetic etiology due to PCDH19 c.918G>A, presenting with focal-to-bilateral tonic-clonic seizures.\n\nPlan:\nContinue current antiseizure medications, zonisamide and lamotrigine, and monitor seizure frequency.",
